      "trivia": "The full bowl is where ramen stops being a recipe and becomes a project, and the component worth the most attention is the egg. An ajitama is a soft-boiled egg with a jammy \u2014 not runny, not set \u2014 yolk, and the timing is unforgiving because it is measured from a fridge-cold egg into water that is already at a rolling boil: six and a half minutes, and thirty seconds either side is a visibly different egg. The ice bath is not optional either, because carryover heat will keep cooking the yolk for another minute if you let it, and by then the window has closed. The last refinement is the finishing torch on the chashu: a blowtorch or a very hot grill for thirty seconds renders the fat cap and blisters the edge, and it is the one restaurant trick that transfers to a home kitchen without any equipment worth arguing about.",
