        "addStep": [{ "text": "Make the curry first \u2014 it is happy to sit while you fry. Cook the sliced onion in the butter over a low heat for a full 30 to 40 minutes, stirring now and then, until it is deep brown, sweet and collapsed. Rushing this is the single reason a home Japanese curry tastes thin. Push the onion aside, stir the extra flour into the butter and cook it for 2 minutes until it smells biscuity, then stir in the curry powder and garam masala and give them 30 seconds in the fat \u2014 dry spice bloomed in fat tastes of something, dry spice dropped into liquid does not. Add the stock a little at a time, whisking each addition smooth before the next, or you will get lumps that never come out. Add the carrot, potato, grated apple and honey, and simmer 25 minutes until the potato is soft and the sauce coats a spoon thickly. Fry and slice the tonkatsu exactly as written, put the rice on one side of the plate and the sliced cutlet next to it, and pour the curry over the RICE and against the edge of the cutlet \u2014 never over the crust." }]
