      "trivia": "Take the pork and the bonito flakes out and the dish barely notices, which tells you something about where its flavour actually comes from: the cabbage, the sauce and the browning. There is one thing to be careful about, and it is invisible. Both the dashi in the batter and the katsuobushi on top are fish, so a vegetarian version has to replace the stock as well as the topping \u2014 using the classic dashi and simply leaving off the flakes is the mistake people make. Use the kombu and shiitake dashi instead, which is a better match here anyway because its woodier depth stands in for the missing pork fat. In place of the bonito on top, a heavier scatter of aonori and some toasted sesame does the work.",
