        "addStep": [{ "text": "Do not mix anything. Thin the batter with an extra 30ml of dashi and spread a very thin crepe, about 18cm across, on the griddle. Dust it with a little aonori, then pile ALL the cabbage and the beansprouts on top in a tall heap \u2014 it will look absurd and it is meant to. Lay the thin pork slices over the heap. Cook 4 minutes, then slide two spatulas underneath and flip the entire tower in one committed movement; if it collapses at the edges, push it back in and carry on. Cover with a lid or a bowl and let it steam 6 to 8 minutes, during which the cabbage will sink to about a third of its height. Meanwhile fry the cooked noodles hard in a little oil on another part of the pan until the edges crisp, shape them into a round the same size as the pancake, and slide the whole tower on top of them. Fry the egg flat, slide the tower onto the egg, and flip the lot one final time so the egg is on top. Sauce, mayonnaise and aonori as usual." }]
